A||N||3||superXmotorsports||4 speed to 5 speed swap||||6
Z||000000||superXmotorsports||09-27-1999||11:26 PM||||Has anybody had any experience with swapping in a 5 speed from a 87 or 88 into an older V6 Fiero?  I want to start a new project (a convertible) and don't need to hack up a GT fastback but it seems impossible to find a 5 speed 86-87 SE or 85 GT.  I've located an 88 4cyl 5 speed and would like to put in an 86 V6 or swap the trans into the 86.  Will the computer work with the 5 speed?  It's a 4 speed car.  Thanks to anybody who can offer advise.||||reg||6
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||09-28-1999||01:10 AM||||I have an 86 2.8 V6 in my 88 coupe with the 88 5spd. The computer (came from an 86 SE V6 4spd) works fine. I think the only thing the computer gets from the tranny is the speed of the car.||||reg||4
Z||000002||DJRice||09-28-1999||08:47 AM||||SCCA is right.  If you do come across a 5 spd with other wiring connections on it (from a Fiero), it probably has the reverse light switch built in, versus mounted at the shifter.<P>I would use the search function and look for transmission swap, because there were several big threads discussing possible donor trannys.||||reg||1
Z||000003||superXmotorsports||09-28-1999||10:21 AM||||Thanks.  The only reason I questioned the computer is because Hypertech and ADS offer a different chip for each 86 4 spd, 86 5 spd, 87 4 spd...etc...||||reg||14
